  "rules": [
    "They're Everywhere (C) and Area 16: at every setup, put all Hollow Men Gather cards on the Infection discard pile.",
    "Cornered (G): leaving a location with 1 or more Hollow Men figures exposes that character.",
    "Hollow Men Gather (S): draw through Gather cards to the first city, add exactly 1 figure, skip supply and plague, and a 4th figure instead drops that city's population by 1 immediately.",
    "Rule T: Gather cards do not count toward the Infect step's draw count. A Gather card drawn in epidemic step 2 is discarded with no effect, then continue to step 3.",
    "Rule W, printed as Game End step c: a location with Hollow Men loses 1 population, and a location with both Hollow Men and Plague cubes still loses only 1.",
    "Area 15 repeats the leave exposure, the 3-figure cap, and the single Game End population drop.",
    "Renewal places an ability worth 2 or less on a character in play, may cover a scar, and is destroyed."
  ],
  "searchResults": {
    "Baghdad": "Gain 2 actions. Hollow Men here are packing cages of rats for another city. Not a companion.",
    "Tehran": "Remove up to 2 Hollow Men figures from the board. Not a companion.",
    "Riyadh": "Immediately take 1 Player card from the discard pile into your hand. The scratch calls Riyadh the Hollow Men headquarters. Not a companion.",
    "Delhi": "Companion Vector Control Technician. No exposure when you begin your turn in an infested city while this card is in your hand.",
    "New Mumbai land": "Gain 1 action. A Hollow Man by the water was drawing his family and crying. Not a companion.",
    "New Mumbai sea": "Lost haven. Open door 65 and add it to the board, or gain 1 action if 65 is already open.",
    "Kolkata": "No search box. Port. The report only suspects a later recon from here."
  },
